{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "Entity taxonomy for the ACTIVE AI language dataset. Each entity type lists: a stable `entity` key (used in the `entities` object of every dataset record), its `value_type`, whether it is a closed enum or an open/free-text vocabulary, and — where applicable — the real backend field/type it is grounded in (src/domain/types.ts) so extracted entities map directly onto real ACTIVE API parameters instead of an invented schema.",
    "grounding_note": "Several fields that look like they should be closed enums are intentionally open free-text strings in the real system (unitType, finishingType, view, orientation) because ACTIVE lets each company/project define its own vocabulary. The entity list below marks these as open_vocabulary and gives common real-world Egyptian-market example values for template generation, without implying the backend restricts them to that list.",
    "franco_variants_note": "location and other proper-noun entities include a franco_variants array with commonly-seen Franco-Arabic / informal-English-transliteration spellings. These are reasonable linguistic variations for generation purposes, not a claim of exhaustively verified real-world usage frequency (see active_ai_dataset_report.md, Section: Data Provenance & Honesty)."
  },
